  "b543c5ae-3a45-486c-8b18-d8c034cfdd17"],
 " is the search."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"2518dfa9-861a-408c-81e7-6322555d2784"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a circle of the band ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component that reaches no further than the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f6a9eab-b492-452d-be17-965d91d43857"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The point form takes the band at ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " and keeps the circles through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". Option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"deltaIn", ",", " ", "deltaOut"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b1cb123-df24-4083-93a3-2062b80dbd68"],
 " widens it to ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["deltaIn", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["deltaOut", "TI"],
 ". A scalar ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "delta"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76859bf9-4a15-479c-a180-4fbd092bb10c"],
 " means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "delta"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7804955-0e56-4f0e-a9bd-619f9ee2d9d6"],
 ", outward only. The default is ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b72ebd06-f08c-4aea-8723-4b4d626ba23e"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d06201a9-1c6e-46ef-a2b3-008d3a8028dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A circle need not exist.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a lattice a single distance shell has no two adjacent vertices, so it \
spans no cycle and the family is empty. Widening the radius to a band fixes \
it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e779c417-384a-4aa2-8719-f1db2ef7803f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21ec7f42-e0a7-4129-828d-d97ae632626c"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe825192-4659-4849-b4fa-160dddf66d87"],
 " of necklaces, cut from the band along a radial seam: a geodesic from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to just outside the band. A necklace is a DAG with one source ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " and one sink ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ". It is the cycle family ",
 StyleBox["opened",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " at its closing arrow ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " -> ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 ", which is left out, so the DAG is acyclic."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"20b24890-935e-472b-b6bd-42770a173413"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is the open chain ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " \[Ellipsis] ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ", read cyclically: a cyclic vertex list whose first vertex is not repeated. \
Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6c522bc-44d1-4129-8b21-f8268fbd0982"],
 " counts the closing edge too, so a circle of ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " vertices has length ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8ffce10c-0861-4813-a029-776279659590"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every member separates. That the necklaces carry every circle exactly once \
needs two hypotheses on the substrate \[LongDash] the winding functional and \
the one-run hypothesis \[LongDash] which nothing here certifies. So ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d546849-3bbd-4da6-9a35-56fb7f217437"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Undetermined"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/Undetermined", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ed0fdbdc-2beb-4d4a-9daf-96407e121fa3"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"95c4e00e-0f23-4b4b-93c4-20af14d35a61"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inside an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d930e0ff-8854-49d1-8df0-af71d9033c63"],
 ", the token ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c130a09-e352-4d5e-9900-c9cea3999638"],
 " still reads ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " as a radius, unlike the head, where a bare second argument is always a \
point. This is an open inconsistency."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f4cc1b6f-5ea0-4c2a-a801-7f83f806d21e"]
}, Open  ]],

